{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And they saw the Elohim of Israel.</b> In a vision and in prophecy." "<b>Like the work of sapphire brick.</b> There is black sapphire, and this is a sapphire of white appearance, and it is like the color of tekhelet — בלו״י in the vernacular. And since sapphire is not recognizable to every person, he went back and gave you a sign for it that is recognizable to all. And what is 'the essence of the heavens for purity'? It is the appearance of the heavens when they are clear and pure of clouds, as it is written: 'and a wind passed and purified them.' <b>לבנת</b> — a term meaning whiteness. Another interpretation: <b>לבנת הספיר</b> — a term for brick. Rabbi Akiva said: Pharaoh's taskmasters were pressing and beating Israel in order to make them produce a quota of bricks in double, as it is written: 'the quota of bricks you shall deliver.' And the Egyptians would not give them straw, and they had to gather stubble in the wilderness, and that stubble was full of thorns and briers, and the straw would pierce their heels, and the blood would be spilt and mixed into the mud. And Rahel, the daughter of Methuselah's grandson, was in labor about to give birth, and she was trampling in the mud with her husband, until the child emerged from her womb and was mixed into the whitening mud, and she cried out over her son, and her cry ascended before the Throne of Glory, and Michael descended and took him and brought him up before the Throne of Glory and made him into a whitener and placed him beneath the feet of the Holy One, blessed be He — this is what is written: 'and beneath His feet like the work of לבנת הספיר.' The meaning: a brick that was made from the sapphire of the woman in labor.'" "<b>And like the essence.</b> A term for appearance, as in 'their appearance is like coral/pearls.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {1 "The midrashic figure 'Rahel daughter of Methuselah's grandson' is translated as read; בלו״י is an unresolved Old French gloss, left untranslated as in the original.", 2 "The scriptural allusion אדמו עצם מפנינים is translated hyper-literally; the reference is uncertain and rendered as it reads."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:00:19.509791999Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}